§§ `s.10(a): each measure, with its preconditions met`

#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `refusal on ground 1` EQUALS (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `refusal on ground 1`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `conditioned renewal on ground 2` EQUALS (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `conditioned renewal on ground 2`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `revocation on ground 3` EQUALS (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `revocation on ground 3`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `restriction on ground 4 for exactly three years` EQUALS (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `restriction on ground 4 for exactly three years`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `suspension on ground 5 for exactly three years` EQUALS (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 5 for exactly three years`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `suspension on ground 6 for three years and a day` EQUALS (LIST `the restriction or suspension runs beyond the three years section 10(a) allows`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 6 for three years and a day`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `suspension on ground 1 up to the clamped third anniversary` EQUALS (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 1 up to the clamped third anniversary`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `suspension on ground 1 beyond the clamped third anniversary` EQUALS (LIST `the restriction or suspension runs beyond the three years section 10(a) allows`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 1 beyond the clamped third anniversary`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `suspension on ground 1 with no period` EQUALS (LIST `the restriction or suspension has no period fixed`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 1 with no period`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `suspension on ground 1 with a period with no end` EQUALS (LIST `the restriction or suspension has no period fixed`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 1 with a period with no end`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `restriction on ground 2 for four years` EQUALS (LIST `the restriction or suspension runs beyond the three years section 10(a) allows`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `restriction on ground 2 for four years`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `suspension on ground 2 for four years` EQUALS (LIST `the restriction or suspension runs beyond the three years section 10(a) allows`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 2 for four years`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `revocation with no ground` EQUALS (LIST `no ground of section 10(a) is made out`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `revocation with no ground`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `revocation without consultation` EQUALS (LIST `the Council was not consulted under section 10`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `revocation without consultation`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `revocation after a consultation whose advice was not valid` EQUALS (LIST `the Council's advice was not validly given under section 10`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `revocation after a consultation whose advice was not valid`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `revocation without a written hearing` EQUALS (LIST `the licensee was not given an opportunity to make claims in writing`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `revocation without a written hearing`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `refusal with a period that does not matter` EQUALS (EMPTY)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `refusal with a period that does not matter`
-- With everything missing: four preconditions unmet, each by membership.
#ASSERT count (`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `revocation with nothing in place`) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT elem `the Council was not consulted under section 10` (`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `revocation with nothing in place`)
#ASSERT elem `the licensee was not given an opportunity to make claims in writing` (`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `revocation with nothing in place`)
#ASSERT elem `no ground of section 10(a) is made out` (`the preconditions of section 10(a) not met` `revocation with nothing in place`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `revocation with nothing in place`

§§ `s.10(a): the three-year cap (P10, a period of validity): IL s.10(c) not applied, and the alternatives`

`a calendar with 1 March 2029 a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2029 3 1
`a calendar with 1 and 2 March 2029 days of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2029 3 1, YMD 2029 3 2
`a calendar with 5 March 2029 a day of rest` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2029 3 5

`a suspension ending on the day after the nominal cap` MEANS `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)` WITH
    `the measure` IS `suspend the licence`
    `the grounds` IS `only ground 5`
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE
    `the period of the restriction or suspension` IS JUST `a period of three years and a day`

`a suspension ending two days after the nominal cap` MEANS `Circumstances of a measure under section 10(a)` WITH
    `the measure` IS `suspend the licence`
    `the grounds` IS `only ground 5`
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE
    `the period of the restriction or suspension` IS JUST `a period of three years and two days`

-- Reading taken: the last day allowed is the third anniversary (IL s.10(b)), no days of rest consulted (the period of validity).
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 5 for exactly three years`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 6 for three years and a day`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension for two years and eleven months`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension for three years and two days`
-- The cap counts the day the period begins as its first day: the last day allowed is the day before the third anniversary.
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap counting the beginning day` `suspension on ground 5 for exactly three years`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap counting the beginning day` `suspension for two years and eleven months`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap counting the beginning day` `suspension on ground 6 for three years and a day`
-- IL s.10(c) applied to the cap (a day of rest at the end moves it to the next day that is not one).
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `suspension on ground 6 for three years and a day`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap moving past days of rest` `suspension on ground 5 for exactly three years` `a calendar with 1 March 2029 a day of rest`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap moving past days of rest` `a suspension ending on the day after the nominal cap` `a calendar with 1 March 2029 a day of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap moving past days of rest` `a suspension ending two days after the nominal cap` `a calendar with 1 March 2029 a day of rest`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap moving past days of rest` `a suspension ending two days after the nominal cap` `a calendar with 1 and 2 March 2029 days of rest`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap moving past days of rest` `a suspension ending on the day after the nominal cap` `a calendar with 5 March 2029 a day of rest`
-- The cap reaches suspensions only: a restriction beyond three years is allowed, a suspension is not.
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `restriction on ground 2 for four years`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap reaching suspensions only` `restriction on ground 2 for four years`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap reaching suspensions only` `suspension on ground 2 for four years`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a), the cap reaching suspensions only` `restriction on ground 4 for exactly three years`

§§ `s.10(a): ground (2) and section 8 (a renewal does not require the s.6(a)(4) condition)`

-- As written, ground (2) is the loss of any condition under s.6 or s.9: a refusal to renew on the loss of the training condition alone is allowed.
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `refusal to renew where only the training condition ceased`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `revocation where only the training condition ceased`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may take the measure under section 10(a)` `refusal to renew where the training condition ceased and ground 3 holds`
