§§ `s.10(b): suspension on an indictment`

`a suspension on an indictment with everything in place` MEANS `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS TRUE
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS TRUE
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE

`a suspension with no indictment` MEANS `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS FALSE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS TRUE
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS TRUE
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE

`a suspension for an offence that does not make the licensee unfit` MEANS `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS FALSE
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS TRUE
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE

`a suspension without a finding of gravity` MEANS `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS TRUE
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS FALSE
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE

`a suspension without consultation` MEANS `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS TRUE
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS TRUE
    `the Council was consulted` IS FALSE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS FALSE
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE

`a suspension after a consultation whose advice was not valid` MEANS `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS TRUE
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS TRUE
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS FALSE
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS TRUE

`a suspension without a written hearing` MEANS `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS TRUE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS TRUE
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS TRUE
    `the Council was consulted` IS TRUE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS TRUE
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS FALSE

`a suspension with nothing in place` MEANS `Circumstances of a suspension under section 10(b)` WITH
    `an indictment was filed against the licensee` IS FALSE
    `in the Registrar's opinion the offence makes the licensee unfit to hold a licence` IS FALSE
    `the Registrar saw that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension` IS FALSE
    `the Council was consulted` IS FALSE
    `the Council's advice was validly given` IS FALSE
    `the licensee was given an opportunity to make claims in writing` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(b) not met` `a suspension on an indictment with everything in place` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment` `a suspension on an indictment with everything in place`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(b) not met` `a suspension with no indictment` EQUALS (LIST `no indictment was filed for an offence as stated in section 6(a)(3)`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment` `a suspension with no indictment`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(b) not met` `a suspension for an offence that does not make the licensee unfit` EQUALS (LIST `no indictment was filed for an offence as stated in section 6(a)(3)`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment` `a suspension for an offence that does not make the licensee unfit`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(b) not met` `a suspension without a finding of gravity` EQUALS (LIST `the Registrar did not find that the gravity of the matter or the public interest requires the suspension`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may suspend the licence until final judgment` `a suspension without a finding of gravity`
