#ASSERT `the Registrar may direct that the licensee not do the specified work until the defect is cured` `a direction on a curable ground 6 defect`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(c) for the direction not met` `a direction with no defect` EQUALS (LIST `no ground of section 10(a) is made out`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may direct that the licensee not do the specified work until the defect is cured` `a direction with no defect`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(c) for the direction not met` `a direction on a defect held not curable` EQUALS (LIST `the Registrar does not hold that the defect can be cured`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may direct that the licensee not do the specified work until the defect is cured` `a direction on a defect held not curable`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(c) for the direction not met` `a direction without consultation` EQUALS (LIST `the Council was not consulted under section 10`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may direct that the licensee not do the specified work until the defect is cured` `a direction without consultation`
#ASSERT `the preconditions of section 10(c) for the direction not met` `a direction after a consultation whose advice was not valid` EQUALS (LIST `the Council's advice was not validly given under section 10`)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may direct that the licensee not do the specified work until the defect is cured` `a direction after a consultation whose advice was not valid`
-- The text names the Council and not a written hearing for this limb: a direction needs no hearing, and the record has no field for one.
